.TH CSTR_INIT_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_init_mp \- initialise a declared cstr using custom memory management
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

cstr_init_mp(s, initial, mprocs);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls cstring_create_full() to initialise the already-declared cstr variable
s with the given initial content and memory management procedures. Calls
fatal_err() if creation fails.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s        cstr variable to initialise (must have been declared)
initial  Initial content (C string or NULL for empty string)
mprocs   Custom memory management procedures (ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Calls fatal_err() on allocation failure
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstr_init (3),
.BR cstr_construct_mp (3),
.BR cstring_create_full (3)
